DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 9

Azure Cloud + Azure DevOps (0–2 Years Experience)

Many enterprises use Microsoft Azure and Azure DevOps extensively.
Interviewers expect you to understand cloud basics + CI/CD workflow on Azure.

📌 Focus: Azure Interview Questions (Mixed – Cloud + DevOps)

• What is Microsoft Azure?
• Azure global infrastructure (Regions & Availability Zones)
• Azure Resource Group – why is it important?
• What is Azure Virtual Machine?
• Difference between Azure VM and AWS EC2
• Azure Storage types (Blob, File, Queue, Table)
• What is Azure Blob Storage used for?
• What is Azure Active Directory (AAD)?
• Difference between AAD and IAM
• What is a Service Principal?
• Azure networking basics (VNet, Subnet)
• What is Network Security Group (NSG)?
• Difference between NSG and Security Group (AWS)
• What is Azure Load Balancer?
• Azure Monitor vs Log Analytics
• What is Azure DevOps?
• Components of Azure DevOps
• What are Azure Repos?
• Azure Repos vs GitHub
• What is Azure Pipeline?
• YAML pipeline vs Classic pipeline
• What is an agent in Azure DevOps?
• Microsoft-hosted vs self-hosted agent
• What are variables in Azure Pipelines?
• How do you store secrets in Azure DevOps?
• What are Azure Artifacts?
• What is a release pipeline?
• How do you deploy to multiple environments using Azure DevOps?
• Common Azure DevOps mistakes beginners make
• Real-world Azure DevOps CI/CD use case

 Interview Tip:
If you explain a simple flow like:
👉 Code → Azure Repo → Pipeline → Build → Release → Deploy
you already sound like a job-ready DevOps engineer, even as a fresher.
